From proto-Slav *slàva, proto-Bal-Sl *ślā́ˀwāˀ: see Lith šlovė̃ “honour, fame”, Lat slava “fame”;
<— PIE *ḱléwos "fame": Gr κλέος "fame" (Κλεοπάτρα "glory of the father"), Welsh clyw "hearing, fame",  Sans श्रवस्  [śrávas] “honor”;
<— PIE *ḱlew- "to hear": слово "word", слух, Ukr слити "to have a reputation for", слишати "to hear", listen, loud, client, Ludwig "loud battle", Hercules, Arm լուր "news";
