Bonus word: кровь
PIE has 2 roots for blood, inside and outside of the body.
Inside: *h₁ésh₂r̥,, associated with life giving and patrilineal line. See Lat saniēs (Fr sang, сангвиник), iron, Arm արյուն.
Outside: *krewh "blood of a wound": aggression, death. See кровь, raw, Lith kraujas, Lat crūdus “raw, bloody” (cruel), Irish cró “violent death", Gr κρέας “flesh” (and pancreas).

So, all 3 words are weird enough to have different origins. I myself find the blood to have the most interesting cognate family.

